<Legal
  title="Privacy · Sway Things"
  description="What sway-things.org does with your data: GitHub Pages serves it and logs your IP address; no cookies, no analytics."
  heading="Privacy"
>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics or tracking, and loads nothing from other servers: its fonts, images
    and scripts all come from sway-things.org. What remains is what any web server needs to deliver a page.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The person named in the <a href="/imprint">imprint</a> is responsible for this website (the controller under the
    GDPR). You can reach them at the email address given there.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting by GitHub Pages</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub B.V., Prins Bernhardplein 200, 1097 JB Amsterdam,
    Netherlands, and of GitHub, Inc., USA. When you open a page, GitHub processes the data your browser sends with every
    request: your IP address, the date and time, the page requested, and your browser and operating system. It does so
    to deliver the page and to protect the service from abuse. GitHub keeps these logs only as long as it needs them for
    that, as its privacy statement describes; the operator of this site has no access to them.
  </p>
  <p>
    You aren't obliged by law or contract to provide this data, but without it your browser can't load the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is the legitimate interest in delivering this site securely and reliably (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). The
    data may be transferred to the USA; GitHub, Inc. is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. Details are
    in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
    >GitHub's General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links and the install command</h2>
  <p>
    Links to the <a href={repo}>source code</a>, the wiki, the issues and the releases lead to GitHub; only when you
    follow one does GitHub's privacy statement apply there. The install command downloads its script from this site, and
    the script then downloads the packages from the openSUSE Build Service, run by SUSE. For those downloads, the <a
      href="https://www.suse.com/company/policies/privacy/"
    >privacy policy of SUSE</a> applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access the data about you, to have it corrected or erased, to restrict its processing, to data
    portability, and to object to its processing (Art. 15 to 21 GDPR). You also have the right to complain to a data
    protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), in particular in the EU member state where you live or work.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site itself stores nothing about you, so it has nothing it could hand out or erase; GitHub's logs are kept by
    GitHub.
  </p>
</Legal>
